<title>SWITZERLAND: Rieter 1996 net profit up 15.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Rieter 1996 net profit up 15.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WINTERTHUR, Switzerland 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to end-1996:</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net			66.3		vs 57.3</p>
<p> Dividend  (Sfr)		9.0		 vs 7.0</p>
<p> Sales			    2,200.4	   vs 2,007.9</p>
<p> Oper result before</p>
<p> interest and taxes	  92.2		vs 71.9</p>
<p> Cash flow			156.4	     vs 136.4</p>
<p> Capital expenditure	  110.3	     vs 83.6</p>
<p> Workforce at year-end	12,320	    vs 12,056</p>
<p> Earnings per share (Sfr)   27.00	     vs 25.81</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of textile machinery and automotive systems maker is Rieter Holding AG. Rieter said in a statement to shareholders that 1996 growth was due primarily to higher sales at the automtive division, which provided slightly over half of total sales, as well as systematic cost management throughout the group.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
